{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-biased action, routes every obstacle event through a dedicated recovery state, uses one-shot backward escape only for front obstacles, prefers directed turns for side obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted by non-critical clear readings, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant sensing from motion capability so specifications can bind sensor outcomes to exactly one motion choice per situation",
    "Use perception states plus one-shot action/recovery states: clear -> move_forward, front obstacle -> move_backward, left obstacle -> rotate_clockwise, right obstacle -> rotate_counterclockwise, with fast return to clear on path_clear"
  ],
